[74/200] Running: How does speculative decoding reduce latency?...

🧠 LLM Response:

A speculative decoding process reduces latency by beginning the decoding of instructions before the processor is certain that they are in the correct order and ready to execute. This allows the processor to begin executing as soon as possible, which can increase performance. If an mispredicted branch is detected, the processor will backtrack and correct the instruction sequence, but the time lost is typically smaller than the time saved by starting execution early. This technique is part of the overall pipeline structure of modern CPUs, designed to maximize efficiency and performance.
