Auto-regressive generation is a method used in machine learning, specifically in language models, to predict and generate sequences of data. Unlike traditional models that generate a sequence of data all at once, auto-regressive models generate data one element at a time.

In auto-regressive generation, each element in the sequence is predicted based on the elements that have already been generated. This is done by training the model on a large dataset and having it learn the statistical dependencies between the elements in the sequence.

For example, in the context of language modeling, an auto-regressive model could be used to predict the next word in a sentence based on the words that have already been predicted. This is useful for applications like chatbots, text generation, and translation.

