Once a model is quantized, it can be generated as a file with the `.tflite` format for Android or `.mMind` for iOS. These files can be served by various frameworks provided by popular smartphone vendors, like Android neural network API (AndroidNNDK), CoreML for iOS and more recently TensorFlow Lite for mobile on both Android and iOS. TensorFlow.js in the browser can also load and run these mobile models with the `@tensorflow/tfjs-node-gpu-plugin` or `@tensorflow/tfjs-backend-webgl` plugins.

